    "text": "The temperature of a body falls from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>minutes</mi></math>, when placed in a constant ambient temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The time it takes for the temperature to fall from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> in the same ambient temperature is",
